This product also includes a neutral harness guardrail whose human-in-the-loop
approval discipline was observed in and generalized from the "PHASE CHECKPOINT"
of those same orchestrators and from the progressive-disclosure agent rule of
rohitg00/awesome-claude-code-toolkit
(https://github.com/rohitg00/awesome-claude-code-toolkit), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0.

This product also includes four neutral lifecycle-hook archetypes whose
event-triggered automation discipline was observed in and generalized from the
hooks of rohitg00/awesome-claude-code-toolkit
(https://github.com/rohitg00/awesome-claude-code-toolkit), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0. The 20 concrete hook scripts are not reproduced; they are
generalized to their lifecycle-event archetype (session-start, pre-tool-use,
post-tool-use, stop).

No source text is copied. Each derived node records its provenance via
dct:source and dct:license. Currently: id:pat-blackboard (Blackboard
coordination), a neutralized coordination pattern abstracted from the
shared-state / durable-artifact handoff recurring across those orchestrators;
id:gr-human-checkpoint (Human approval checkpoint), a neutralized
human-in-the-loop approval gate abstracted from the phase-checkpoint /
progressive-disclosure discipline recurring across both sources above; and
id:hook-session-start / id:hook-pre-tool-use / id:hook-post-tool-use /
id:hook-stop (lifecycle hooks), neutralized event-trigger archetypes abstracted
from the toolkit's SessionStart / PreToolUse / PostToolUse / Stop hooks.
